You can set a merge strategy option so git auto-resolves conflicts in favor of the incoming branch, with no manual step:

bash
git merge -X theirs main
To make this the default for all future merges in this repo, add it to your git config:

bash
git config merge.ours.driver true   # not needed for this, ignore
git config pull.rebase false
git config merge.strategy recursive
git config merge.strategyOption theirs
Actually, the cleanest way to bake it in permanently is a repo-level alias:

bash
git config alias.mergetheirs '!git merge -X theirs'

Then just run git mergetheirs main instead of git merge main.

Or, if you want git merge itself (no custom command) to always behave this way, add this to .git/config:

ini
[merge]
    ours = false
    strategyOption = theirs